-- title:
--   Closed points above a supersingular place carry no q-torsion
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$.
--
--   **Data over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.** Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. the image of $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A, M') = \kappa_A(j(\mathsf q), j(\mathsf q^{M'})) \subset \kappa_A((\mathsf q))$ over $\kappa_A :=$ `ResidueField A` (a place being a valuation subring containing the image of the base field, distinct from the whole field, and a principal ideal ring), and let `hW` say that $W$ consists exactly of the places satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace q M'`, that is, $W = \mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'\,\kappa_A$. The hypothesis `hle` requires the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; here the left side is the subfield generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise images of the elements of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M' = \mathbb Q(\mathrm{divisorExpansions}\,M')$, and the right side is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')`, where $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ along $A$ with target $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa_A,M')$: it consists of a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective ring homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ from it onto the target whose kernel is its maximal ideal, and a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places, subject to the conditions that an element of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is in $A$ exactly when its image is integral, that $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ extends the residue map of $A$, that every nonzero element becomes integral with nonzero residue after scaling by a constant, that $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ preserves degrees, and that divisors of elements with nonzero residue push forward to divisors of residues. The hypothesis `hR₀` is the compatibility with $q$-expansions: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that element is $R_0$-integral, and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Finally, $s$ is an element of $W$.
--
--   **The small constant field.** Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ an element lying in $A$ (`hπ`), and write $A_0 :=$ `A.comap (algebraMap ↥k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))` for the induced valuation subring of $k_0$. The hypotheses on $A_0$ are: `hdvr`, that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring; `hunif`, that its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$; `hhens`, that it is a henselian local ring; `hres`, that its residue field is algebraically closed; and `hκ`, that every element $a \in A$ is congruent, modulo the maximal ideal of $A$, to (the image of) some $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **The auxiliary prime and the field $K$.** Let $\ell'$ be a prime with $\ell' \ne q$, $3 \le \ell'$ and $\ell' \nmid M'$, and let $\xi \in k_0$ be a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity (`hξ`) which is normalised in the sense of `hιξ`: there exists a ring homomorphism $\iota : k_0 \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota(\xi) = \exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $k_0((\mathsf q))$ over $k_0$ with, by `hK`, $K = \mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,k_0\,\big(\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,((q\ell')^2M')\,(\mathrm{levelH}\,(q\ell')\,M')\big)$, i.e. generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansion function field at level $(q\ell')^2M'$ for the subgroup of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times$ of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell'$; $K$ is an $A_0$-algebra compatibly with $k_0$. Let $j \in K$ be the element whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image in $k_0((\mathsf q))$ of $\mathrm{jq}$, the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant (`hj`), and assume $j \ne 0$.
--
--   **Guards on the moduli data.** The hypothesis `hℓ` requires that for every commutative $A_0$-algebra $T$, Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, variable change $C$ and `LevelPData` $D$ (a quadruple of coordinates $x_P, y_P, x_Q, y_Q$), if $D$ is a level-$\ell'$ structure on $W$ (both points satisfy the Weierstrass equation, both abscissae kill $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell'}$, and the two independence elements are units) then $D.\mathrm{variableChange}\,C$ is a level-$\ell'$ structure on $C \bullet W$. The hypothesis `hM` requires the analogous equivariance for $\mathrm{IsGamma0PowAt}\,W\,p\,k\,h$ (which is `W.IsTwoKernel h` when $p^k = 2$ and `W.IsCyclicGenKernel p k h` otherwise), the transformed polynomial being $\mathrm{kernelVariableChangeDeg}\,C\,(\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\,p\,k)\,h$. Further, $\mathcal G$ is a family `GroupLaws A₀` of relative group laws on projective Weierstrass models over $A_0$-algebras, assumed chord-and-tangent (`h𝒢`: each law admits a points-evaluation) and origin-normalised (`h𝒢O`: each identity section is cut out by a ring homomorphism on the origin chart killing the two affine coordinates); $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport A₀ 𝒢 q`, functorially transporting raw Drinfeld pairs along $A_0$-algebra maps and variable changes and preserving the level condition, assumed to be a section transport (`h𝒯`: the transported sections agree with the original ones after the canonical identifications, in both the variable-change and the base-change direction). The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every $A_0$-algebra $T$ and projective Weierstrass curve over $T$, graded ring homomorphisms realising a variable change, respectively the base change along an $A_0$-algebra map, on the graded coordinate rings of the projective models, each carrying the irrelevant ideal appropriately and satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom`, respectively `IsCoefficientHom`.
--
--   Write $\mathcal R := \mathrm{rigidDataPow}\,A_0\,\ell'\,M'\,q\,h_\ell\,h_M\,\mathcal G\,\mathcal T$ for the rigid Weierstrass datum obtained from the product of the $\Gamma_0$-power component at level $M'$, the level-$\ell'$ component and the level-$q$ Drinfeld component, and $\mathcal D := \mathcal R.\mathrm{toLevelModuliDatum}$ for the associated moduli datum, whose points over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ are the raw data (a Weierstrass curve with unit discriminant together with a level structure) modulo variable change, with $j$-invariant map $\mathrm{jOf}$.
--
--   **The universal point and the chart.** Let $P_0$ be a `LevelModuliPackageAbs` for $\mathcal D$ over $A_0$: an $A_0$-algebra $P_0.B_0$ with a point $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ over it such that every point of $\mathcal D$ over an $A_0$-algebra $T$ is the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under a unique $A_0$-algebra map. Let $x_0$ be a point of $\mathcal D$ over $K$ whose $j$-invariant has Laurent series $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,(q\ell') = \mathrm{qExpand}\,(q\ell')$ applied to the modular invariant over $k_0$ (`hx₀`). Write $\mathcal O := \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,A_0\,K\,j$ for the $A_0$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A_0[j]$, and let $\mathrm{clC} : P_0.B_0 \to \mathcal O$ be an $A_0$-algebra map whose composite with the inclusion $\mathcal O \hookrightarrow K$ is the classifying map $P_0.\mathrm{classify}\,x_0$ of $x_0$ (`hclC`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** For every maximal ideal $y$ of $\mathcal O$ and every $A_0$-algebra homomorphism $\psi : \mathcal O \to$ `ResidueField A₀` whose vanishing locus is exactly $y$ (that is, $\psi(c) = 0$ if and only if $c \in y$), the following implication holds.
--
--   Suppose that $y$ lies over the place $s$ in the following sense: for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ belonging to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ is $R_0$-integral, such that (i) at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $\mathrm{jq}$ one also has $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $g$, and (ii) the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$, and such that $\mathrm{qExpand}\,k_0\,\ell'$ applied to the coefficientwise image of $g$ lies in $K$ and the resulting element of $K$ lies in $\mathcal O$, one has: for every $c \in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\kappa_A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference in $\mathcal O$ between that element and the image of $c$ under $A_0 \to \mathcal O$ lies in $y$.
--
--   Then for every raw datum $x$ of $\mathcal R$ over `ResidueField A₀` whose class in $\mathcal R.\mathrm{Pt}(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A_0)$ equals the image of $P_0.\mathrm{univ}$ under $\mathcal D.\mathrm{map}$ of $\psi \circ \mathrm{clC}$, and for every point $P$ of the affine curve underlying $x.\mathrm{curve}$, the relation $q \cdot P = 0$ forces $P = 0$.
--
--   The statement is the supersingularity assertion for the fibre of the integral model of the full-level modular curve at a closed point lying above a supersingular place $s$ in characteristic $q$: the elliptic curve classified there has no nonzero $q$-torsion point over the (algebraically closed) residue field, so it is supersingular. It is used in the further analysis of such closed points, in particular by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_place_forall_isModuliPlaceOf_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_place_forall_isModuliPlaceOf_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint), [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.moduliPoint_mk_eq_of_forall_apply_qExpand_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.moduliPoint_mk_eq_of_forall_apply_qExpand_eq_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.natCard_variableChange_act_curve_eq_and_level_fst_eq_eq_two_mul_placeWidthChar_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.natCard_variableChange_act_curve_eq_and_level_fst_eq_eq_two_mul_placeWidthChar_of_over_of_eq_map_classify_rigidDataPow_of_tatePoint).
